{"id": "EUVD-2026-103906", "enisaUuid": "60fbeace-ed7f-3827-96e2-1578884b118c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblock: reject polled dio with user integrity metadata\n\nIOCB_HAS_METADATA leaves iocb->private as a uio_meta, while\niocb_bio_iopoll() expects a bio. Since 2729a60bbfb9, metadata I/O\nalways uses __blkdev_direct_IO(), which never publishes the bio for\npolling, so IOPOLL calls bio_poll() on the uio_meta.\n\nReproducer: io_uring IOPOLL plus a PI attribute on an integrity device\n(scsi_debug dif=1 dix=1). KASAN reports:\n\n  Oops: general protection fault, probably for non-canonical\n  address 0xdffffc0000000004\n  KASAN: null-ptr-deref in range\n  [0x0000000000000020-0x0000000000000027]\n  RIP: 0010:bio_poll+0x9d/0x4b0\n  Call Trace:\n   iocb_bio_iopoll+0x5b/0x80\n   io_uring_classic_poll+0xf3/0x140\n   io_do_iopoll+0x4e3/0xc00\n   io_iopoll_check+0x275/0x560\n   __do_sys_io_uring_enter+0x2e5/0x720\n\nReturn -EOPNOTSUPP when HIPRI is combined with user metadata.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:49:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:26:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c97ef13ad96be0e08af38dfa2ed40cded0b53e1b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd33c03cefccdfcb223e9e6262643d64f8c1ae20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a42e6fe1293f2e2d579c9fe5bbab056dd8b880e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4mqf-mrhr-h3rh", "CVE-2026-98821"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "22fe7431-da61-37c1-94d6-7060ca251eb6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3c198af1-8482-32fa-be86-19bac5392874", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2729a60bbfb9215997f25372ebe9b7964f038296 <dd33c03cefccdfcb223e9e6262643d64f8c1ae20"}, {"id": "768ecb5f-558b-31f3-afca-d5549f26baa0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2729a60bbfb9215997f25372ebe9b7964f038296 <2a42e6fe1293f2e2d579c9fe5bbab056dd8b880e"}, {"id": "8bd528d2-84b8-3d65-834d-f0b3dc5963c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16.8 <6.17"}, {"id": "90f61231-09ae-3166-ad20-d9dbc1554c25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a729700e-31f4-364e-8f11-3f4be17448fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "bc59dfb5-33f5-3945-8bdf-e2f849fe0e01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "17ecefc9fdd8c554e0d03e5a990daef19f930add"}, {"id": "ce3060e8-b66c-35f5-9ad7-4e00224ab769", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2729a60bbfb9215997f25372ebe9b7964f038296 <c97ef13ad96be0e08af38dfa2ed40cded0b53e1b"}, {"id": "d7154a51-18f3-3578-a3bb-8072167ae99a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "da271fb7-fa3d-3b04-8b46-1b1fe254e223", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b658a650-8462-3bd6-a9d2-462b0c771abe", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}